--TEST--
a literal is a value and not a body, so the cursor inside one is answered as the position around it — which is what an interpolation slot needs, the variables in scope being exactly what may be written there, `rule:ide/the-request-set-is-closed`
--FILE--
<?nvs
string $name = "world";
echo "he<|>llo";
--REQUEST--
completion prefix=$
--EXPECT--
$name   variable  string
